 "title": "Kinship terms",
 "hook": "Kinbank is a browseable and downloadable database of family-tree nomenclature for 1,000+ spoken languages, across 100+ types of relationships. Examples include ahätatum (Akkadian for one’s younger sister), yerudê (Galibi Carib for one’s husband’s brother’s wife), and ɗan’ùbā (Hausa for one’s paternal half-brother).",
